title: Social welfare policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: social_welfare_timer = 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: psoe_in_government = 1 and social_welfare_timer = 0
card-image: img/placeholder.jpg

= Social Welfare Policy

The Instituto Nacional de Previsión administers Spain's patchwork welfare state - the old-age and disability pension scheme (*retiro obrero*), maternity insurance, and workers' accident compensation. Expanding it has been a proud achievement of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> participation in government, but there is continuous pressure to scale it back[? if black_thursday_seen = 1 :, especially given the economic crisis ?].

- @reduce_spending: Reduce spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending_pre_depression: Increase spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending_post_depression: Increase spending (welfare levels will remain about the same).
- @spending_same_pre_depression: Keep spending the same.
- @spending_same_post_depression: Keep spending the same (effectively a service cut).
- @easy_discard
#- @cancel_advisor_action

@reduce_spending
subtitle: This will hurt our proletarian base. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; industrial_psoe -= 6; unemployed_psoe -= 6; industrial_pce += 3; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; radical_relation += 5; izq_rep_relation += 2; ceda_relation += 3; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if (in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front) and coalition_dissent > 0; pce_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have reduced levels of social welfare spending. This means more poverty and suffering for the working class. Our detractors claim we are sacrificing proletarian livelihoods for the sake of class peace with the propertied classes. Are they wrong? Are the workers wrong to turn to the <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span>, in light of our choices?


@increase_spending_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

We have increased welfare spending. Our proletarian base is pleased.

@increase_spending_post_depression
view-if: unemployed > 15
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 0; inflation += 0.3;
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid to maintain the same benefits. -1 Budget

Increasing welfare spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we are essentially treading water.

@spending_same_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15

We have kept welfare spending the same.


@spending_same_post_depression
view-if: unemployed > 15
on-arrival: industrial_psoe -= 3; unemployed_psoe -= 4; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; pce_relation -= 8 if in_popular_front
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid.

Maintaining spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we have essentially cut welfare in real terms. The workers are justifiably displeased - we are sacrificing their livelihoods to appease demands for austerity.

[? if in_popular_front: The <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> is turning against us over our welfare policy. ?]
